\\": normalized_gain_rounded\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that processes a case payload as described. The payload has \"threshold\" and \"calls\". Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable.\n\nWe need to compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call, then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens. Then accepted if parseable is True and normalized_gain >= threshold. Then create diagnostics array with call_id, accepted boolean, normalized_gain rounded? The instruction says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". What rounding? Probably round to some standard? The specification doesn't specify number of decimal places. But in the output schema, normalized_gain is number (float). The examples? There are no expected outputs given. But likely we should keep as computed float, maybe round to a reasonable number? The prompt says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but later \"Return only JSON-serializable values\". Possibly we need to round to some precision? In the diagnostics, normalized_gain is a number, can be any float. I think we should just compute and leave as float, no rounding specified. However the instruction says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - could be that we need to round to 6 decimal places? Not sure. Look at candidate_artifact: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" It also says \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\". I think we should round to a reasonable precision, maybe 6 decimal places? But to be safe, since the output schema says type: number, we can just leave as float. However the original call values have many decimal places. Many tasks require rounding to avoid floating point artifacts. Since it says \"rounded\", I will round to 6 decimal places. But that may be arbitrary. Let's see if the fixture payload has many digits. They have up to 8 decimal places. I'll round to 6 decimal places. Actually, better to see if there is any hint. In the candidate_artifact: \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" and \"Return only JSON-serializable values with the exact named fields.\" So I'll round to 6 decimal places using round(x, 6). Or maybe we need to preserve as is? The candidate_artifact says \"rounded\" explicitly. I'll implement rounding to 6 decimal places. \n\nAlso, return accepted_call_ids list of strings in order of accepted calls? The order: \"Keep diagnostics in supplied call order.\" So diagnostics should be in the order of calls in the input. accepted_call_ids should also be in that order? Probably yes, list of call_ids of accepted calls in the original order. So we iterate calls in order, compute, collect accepted call_ids, and build diagnostics list.\n\nNow, implementation must not mutate case. So work on a copy? Not needed, just read from it.\n\nWe need to raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. Cases from fixture are valid. But we should check types and presence of required fields: threshold should be number, calls should be list, each call has required fields. If any missing, raise ValueError.\n\nThe function must be Python source as a string. So we'll write a function.\n\nNow, output envelope: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n ...\"} with proper escaping.\n\nI'll write the code.\n\nEdge cases: prediction_tokens could be zero? Then gain/prediction_tokens would be division by zero. We should check and treat as not acceptable? Or maybe invalid case. Since threshold is inclusive, normalized_gain must be >= threshold. If tokens=0, gain maybe positive? But impossible. We'll raise ValueError if prediction_tokens <=0? Actually, it's unlikely, but to be safe, we can treat as not parseable? The spec says \"For each call subtract loss with the call from loss without it. Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" That suggests prediction_tokens must be >=1. If zero, it's invalid. Raise ValueError.\n\nNow, rounding: I'll round to 6 decimal places. But the accepted normalized_gain for diagnostics? The spec says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". The accepted_call_ids list is just strings. So rounding.\n\nNow produce code.\n\nI'll write:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"threshold\" not in case or \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing threshold or calls\")\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be number\")\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be list\")\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"call must be dict\")\n        # check required fields\n        for key in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if key not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"missing {key} in call\")\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive int\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be bool\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        # round to 6 decimal places\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 6)\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain_rounded >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat should satisfy.\n\nNow, output as JSON with key \"implementation\". Ensure proper escaping.\n\nLet me produce the JSON string."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":1828,"total_tokens":3999,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1332},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}